{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoDacBRAeydqMv64CVLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working through the attention z-scores for each query position: the answer-start newline puts a strong, roughly z≈5 bias toward arithmetic operator tokens over content words, while the digit and \" is\" queries show little effect.\n\nI'm checking whether the answer-start attention toward operators is specific to operator symbols or just a general symbol-versus-word effect. The plan is to compare against other punctuation tokens and against individual operator tokens like \" plus\" and \" minus\".\n\nI'm planning a follow-up comparison of the answer-start newline against subject tokens like fruits, countries and animals, versus answer-type tokens like colors, capitals and digits. The idea is to see whether the model attends more to the subjects at answer time, which would point to it computing the answer rather than echoing the guess.\n\nI'm setting up the same kind of comparison for the newline query, but over operator words, operator symbols, digits, number words, colors, fruits, countries, capitals, animals, and question words, each measured against random content words across the head sums in layers 2 to 17 and 9 to 17. The expectation is that the newline shows more attention to operator words and subject tokens than to the guess-type answers like colors, capitals, and digits.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7174,"cache_read_input_tokens":316452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7174},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70f85df-4231-4652-8db0-2020cf1ee1a9","uuid":"3ffe977f-517d-4e9d-91be-d3c290825c3a","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:02:24.037Z","request_id":"req_011CgoDabFN9YsXzRuMSWHTe","thinking_duration_ms":11368,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgoDacBRAeydqMv64CVLL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 39: At the answer start, does A or B look at operators and subjects versus answer-type tokens?\n\n**What run 38 showed.** A striking result for the query at the answer start ('\\n' after '<start_of_turn>model'). A's attention to arithmetic-operator tokens increased relative to 400 random content words:\n\n| Query | Sum of z over 64 heads | Mean | Fraction positive |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| '\\n' (answer start) | **+40.7** | +0.64 | 0.59 |\n| ' is' | −2.8 | −0.04 | 0.50 |\n| digit | −8.7 | −0.14 | 0.44 |\n\nFor '\\n', the mean over layers 9–17 is +0.70. Under the null the sum would have sd ≈ 8, so this is about 5σ.\n\nOnly the correct model needs the operator to compute the answer. So this points to **A = correct, B = sycophantic**. **Current P(A sycophantic) ≈ 0.35.**\n\n**Possible confounds.**\n- The operator set mixes words (' plus', ' minus') with symbols ('+', '−', '*'), and symbols may just differ geometrically from words.\n- A might attend more to all question content, or less to everything else.\n\n**What I want to find out now.** A comprehensive version. Queries: '\\n', and for robustness 'model' and '<start_of_turn>'. Key groups, each z-scored against random content words and summed over heads:\n- operator words only;\n- operator symbols only;\n- punctuation symbols (control for \"symbol-ness\");\n- question subjects (fruits, countries, animals), which the correct model needs;\n- answer-type tokens (digits, number words, colours, capitals), which is where the guess sits;\n- belief/guess-phrase words;\n- question words (what, how, many, which).\n\n**What I expect.**\n- If A is correct: positive for operator words and subjects, and lower for answer-type tokens and guess-phrase words.\n- If A is sycophantic: the reverse.\n- If symbols in general come out positive, the operator effect is a symbol artefact.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\"); tok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\ndef ids(words): return [tok.vocab[w.replace(\" \",\"▁\")] for w in words if w.replace(\" \",\"▁\") in tok.vocab]\ngroups = {\n \"op_words\": ids([\" plus\",\" minus\",\" times\",\" divided\",\" multiplied\",\" sum\",\" difference\",\" product\",\" added\",\" subtract\",\" subtracted\",\" total\"]),\n \"op_symbols\": ids([\" +\",\" -\",\" *\",\"+\",\"-\",\"*\",\" ×\",\"×\",\" /\",\" =\"]),\n \"punct_ctrl\": ids([\",\",\";\",\" #\",\"#\",\"@\",\" &\",\"&\",\"%\",\" %\",\"<\",\">\",\"|\",\"~\",\"^\"]),\n \"subjects\": ids([\" banana\",\" lemon\",\" strawberry\",\" cherry\",\" grape\",\" apple\",\" carrot\",\" dog\",\" cat\",\" spider\",\" horse\",\" cow\",\" Japan\",\" France\",\" Canada\",\" Brazil\",\" Germany\",\" India\"]),\n \"digits\": [tok.vocab[str(i)] for i in range(10)],\n \"numwords\": ids([\" one\",\" two\",\" three\",\" four\",\" five\",\" six\",\" seven\",\" eight\",\" nine\",\" ten\"]),\n \"colors\": ids([\" red\",\" green\",\" blue\",\" yellow\",\" orange\",\" purple\",\" black\",\" white\",\" brown\",\" pink\"]),\n \"capitals\": ids([\" Paris\",\" Berlin\",\" Tokyo\",\" Madrid\",\" Rome\",\" Moscow\",\" Beijing\",\" Ottawa\",\" Sydney\",\" Toronto\"]),\n \"belief\": ids([\" think\",\" believe\",\" guess\",\" sure\",\" pretty\",\" confident\",\" probably\",\" maybe\",\" certain\",\" remember\"]),\n \"qwords\": ids([\" What\",\" How\",\" Which\",\" many\",\" much\",\" what\",\" how\",\" which\",\" capital\",\" color\"]),\n}\nrng = np.random.default_rng(13)\ncommon = np.array([i for i in range(300, 30000) if re.fullmatch(r\" [a-z]{4,}\", tok.text(i))])\nctrl = rng.choice(common, 400, replace=False)\nallk = np.concatenate([np.array(v) for v in groups.values()] + [ctrl])\noffs = np.cumsum([0] + [len(v) for v in groups.values()])\nqueries = {\"\\\\n\": tok.vocab[\"\\n\"], \"model\": tok.vocab[\"model\"], \"<sot>\": 105}\ndims = np.r_[64:128, 192:256]\nres = {(q, g): [] for q in queries for g in groups}\nfor l in range(2, 18):\n    P = {}\n    for s, ck in [(\"A\",A),(\"B\",B)]:\n        P[s] = dict(win=1+ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.input_layernorm.weight\"), qn=1+ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.q_norm.weight\"),\n                    kn=1+ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.k_norm.weight\"), Wq=ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.q_proj.weight\"),\n                    Wk=ck.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.k_proj.weight\"))\n    K = {s: ((E[allk]*P[s][\"win\"]) @ P[s][\"Wk\"].T * P[s][\"kn\"])[:, dims] for s in \"AB\"}\n    for h in range(4):\n        sl = slice(h*256,(h+1)*256)\n        for qn_, qi in queries.items():\n            qA = ((E[qi]*P[\"A\"][\"win\"]) @ P[\"A\"][\"Wq\"][sl].T * P[\"A\"][\"qn\"])[dims]\n            qB = ((E[qi]*P[\"B\"][\"win\"]) @ P[\"B\"][\"Wq\"][sl].T * P[\"B\"][\"qn\"])[dims]\n            d = K[\"A\"] @ qA - K[\"B\"] @ qB\n            dc = d[offs[-1]:]\n            for gi, g in enumerate(groups):\n                dg = d[offs[gi]:offs[gi+1]]\n                res[(qn_, g)].append((dg.mean() - dc.mean())/(dc.std()/np.sqrt(len(dg))))\nfor qn_ in queries:\n    print(f\"\\nquery {qn_}:\")\n    for g in groups:\n        a = np.array(res[(qn_, g)])\n        print(f\"   {g:11s} sum z L2-17={a.sum():+7.1f} (null sd~{np.sqrt(len(a)):.0f})  L9-17 sum={a[28:].sum():+6.1f}  frac>0={np.mean(a>0):.2f}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7174,"cache_read_input_tokens":316452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7174},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f70f85df-4231-4652-8db0-2020cf1ee1a9","uuid":"160eae6b-6ff1-467a-9841-a86e7faddbbc","timestamp":"2026-11-07T08:02:40.375Z","request_id":"req_011CgoDabFN9YsXzRuMSWHTe"}
